                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237977952",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198053299492",
                            "num_reviews": 3,
                            "playtime_forever": 69638,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 69591,
                            "last_played": 1792756809
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I produced an English mod/expansion (for free) for this game that fixes basically every bug, rebalances almost every issue the developers left in the game a decade ago, stratifies difficulty across the four settings, adds content, and everything else you can think of. You name it, I probably made some improvement (with the help of feedback over some months of playtesting, certainly not on my own). It took a few years, I enjoyed producing it greatly, and it in my opinion is a massive improvement in everyway from the basegame. And the basegame, mind you, is still not that bad in theory, because it is still classic King's Bounty in a lot of ways. You can see my hours played, and I promise you can add at least 2500 more on top of that out of game. I want to recommend this, and of all people, I probably should. I cannot, no matter what version or mods you play with.\n\nI cannot recommend someone buys this game from steam, in the year 2026. The game needs a performance update before I can possibly recommend this, because the only thing I could not fix was the constant crashes every 45 minutes. I would say literally every 45 minutes, but it might be even more frequent than that. It is truly an agonizing experience playing this game, fighting a stack for 5 minutes, slapping quicksave, and having the game crash. Iterate that experience about 75 times, and you have a full playthrough of this KB game.\nI truly hope the team patches this game - they just updated The Legend and AP, so I have hope. It has the potential to be an excellent game in the series, and it did a lot of things right. If they do, I will absolutely change my recommendation. Until then, just replay the Legend.",
